\p \v 15 \w So the Israelite|strong="H01121"\w* \w foremen|strong="H07860"\w* \w went|strong="H00935"\w* \w and appealed|strong="H06817"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Pharaoh|strong="H06547"\w*: “\w Why|strong="H04100"\w* \w are you treating|strong="H06213"\w* \w your servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w this way|strong="H03541"\w*? \v 16 \w No|strong="H00369"\w* \w straw|strong="H08401"\w* \w has been given|strong="H05414"\w* \w to your servants|strong="H05650"\w*, \w yet we are told|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w Make|strong="H06213"\w* \w bricks|strong="H03843"\w*!’ \w Look|strong="H02009"\w*, \w your servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w are being beaten|strong="H05221"\w*, \w but the fault|strong="H02398"\w* \w is with your own people|strong="H05971"\w*.”
