\s1 The Waters of Marah
\p \v 22 \w Then Moses|strong="H04872"\w* \w led|strong="H05265"\w* \w Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w from the Red|strong="H05488"\w* \w Sea|strong="H03220"\w*, \w and they went out|strong="H03318"\w* \w into|strong="H00413"\w* \w the Desert|strong="H04057"\w* \w of Shur|strong="H07793"\w*. \w For three|strong="H07969"\w* \w days|strong="H03117"\w* \w they walked|strong="H01980"\w* \w in the desert|strong="H04057"\w* \w without|strong="H03808"\w* \w finding|strong="H04672"\w* \w water|strong="H04325"\w*. \v 23 \w And when they came|strong="H00935"\w* \w to Marah|strong="H04785"\w*,\f + \fr 15:23 \fqa Marah \ft means \fqa bitter\ft .\f* \w they could|strong="H03201"\w* \w not|strong="H03808"\w* \w drink|strong="H08354"\w* \w the water|strong="H04325"\w* \w there|strong="H04785"\w* \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w it|strong="H01992"\w* \w was bitter|strong="H04751"\w*. (\w That is why|strong="H05921"\w* \w it was named|strong="H07121"\w* \w Marah|strong="H04785"\w*.)
\p \v 24 \w So the people|strong="H05971"\w* \w grumbled|strong="H03885"\w* \w against|strong="H05921"\w* \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w*, \w saying|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w What|strong="H04100"\w* \w are we to drink|strong="H08354"\w*?” \v 25 \w And Moses cried out|strong="H06817"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \w and the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w showed him|strong="H03384"\w* \w a log|strong="H06086"\w*. \w And when he cast it|strong="H07993"\w* \w into|strong="H00413"\w* \w the waters|strong="H04325"\w*, \w they|strong="H04325"\w* \w were sweetened|strong="H04985"\w*.
