\p \v 22 \w On the sixth|strong="H08345"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w*, \w they gathered|strong="H03950"\w* \w twice|strong="H04932"\w* \w as much food|strong="H03899"\w* — \w two|strong="H08147"\w* \w omers|strong="H06016"\w* \w per person|strong="H00259"\w*\f + \fr 16:22 \fqa 2 omers \ft is approximately 4 dry quarts or 4.4 liters per person.\f* — \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the leaders|strong="H05387"\w* \w of the congregation|strong="H05712"\w* \w came|strong="H00935"\w* \w and reported|strong="H05046"\w* \w this to Moses|strong="H04872"\w*. \v 23 \w He told them|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w This|strong="H01931"\w* \w is what|strong="H00834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w has said|strong="H01696"\w*: ‘\w Tomorrow|strong="H04279"\w* \w is to be a day of complete rest|strong="H07677"\w*, \w a holy|strong="H06944"\w* \w Sabbath|strong="H07676"\w* \w to the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*. \w So|strong="H00853"\w* \w bake|strong="H00644"\w* \w what|strong="H00834"\w* \w you want to bake|strong="H00644"\w*, \w and|strong="H00853"\w* \w boil|strong="H01310"\w* \w what|strong="H00834"\w* \w you want to boil|strong="H01310"\w*. \w Then set aside|strong="H05117"\w* \w whatever|strong="H03605"\w* \w remains|strong="H05736"\w* \w and keep it|strong="H04931"\w* \w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w morning|strong="H01242"\w*.’”
