\p \v 31 \w Now the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w called the bread|strong="H07121"\w* \w manna|strong="H04478"\w*.\f + \fr 16:31 \fqa Manna \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa What is it? \ft (see verse 15).\f* \w It|strong="H01931"\w* \w was white|strong="H03836"\w* \w like coriander|strong="H01407"\w* \w seed|strong="H02233"\w* \w and tasted|strong="H02940"\w* \w like wafers|strong="H06838"\w* \w made with honey|strong="H01706"\w*. \v 32 \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w This|strong="H02088"\w* \w is what|strong="H00834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w has commanded|strong="H06680"\w*: ‘\w Keep|strong="H04931"\w* \w an omer|strong="H06016"\w* \w of manna|strong="H04480"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H01755"\w*, \w so that|strong="H04616"\w* \w they may see|strong="H07200"\w* \w the bread|strong="H03899"\w* \w I fed|strong="H00398"\w* \w you in the wilderness|strong="H04057"\w* \w when I brought you|strong="H03318"\w* \w out of the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w*.’”
