\p \v 1 \w Then the whole|strong="H03605"\w* \w congregation|strong="H05712"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w left|strong="H05265"\w* \w the Desert|strong="H04057"\w* \w of Sin|strong="H05512"\w*,\f + \fr 17:1 \ft The geographical name \fqa Sin \ft is related to \fqa Sinai \ft and should not be mistaken for the English word \fqa sin\ft .\f* \w moving from place to place|strong="H04550"\w* \w as|strong="H05921"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w commanded|strong="H06310"\w*. \w They camped|strong="H02583"\w* \w at Rephidim|strong="H07508"\w*, \w but there was no|strong="H00369"\w* \w water|strong="H04325"\w* \w for the people|strong="H05971"\w* \w to drink|strong="H08354"\w*. \v 2 \w So the people|strong="H05971"\w* \w contended|strong="H07378"\w* \w with|strong="H05973"\w* \w Moses|strong="H04872"\w*, “\w Give|strong="H05414"\w* us \w water|strong="H04325"\w* \w to drink|strong="H08354"\w*.”
