\p \v 14 \w Three|strong="H07969"\w* \w times|strong="H07272"\w* \w a year|strong="H08141"\w* \w you are to celebrate a feast|strong="H02287"\w* to Me.
\p \v 15 \w You are to keep|strong="H08104"\w* \w the Feast|strong="H02282"\w* \w of Unleavened Bread|strong="H04682"\w*\f + \fr 23:15 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see Exodus 12:14–20.\f* \w as|strong="H00834"\w* \w I commanded you|strong="H06680"\w*: \w At the appointed time|strong="H04150"\w* \w in the month|strong="H02320"\w* \w of Abib|strong="H00024"\w*\f + \fr 23:15 \fqa Abib \ft was the first month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April.\f* \w you are to eat|strong="H00398"\w* \w unleavened bread|strong="H04682"\w* \w for seven|strong="H07651"\w* \w days|strong="H03117"\w*, \w because|strong="H03588"\w* that was the month \w you came out|strong="H03318"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w*. \w No one|strong="H03808"\w* \w may appear|strong="H07200"\w* \w before Me|strong="H06440"\w* \w empty-handed|strong="H07387"\w*.
