\p \v 16 \w The Israelites|strong="H01121"\w* \w must keep|strong="H08104"\w* \w the Sabbath|strong="H07676"\w*, \w celebrating|strong="H06213"\w* \w it|strong="H07676"\w* \w as a permanent|strong="H05769"\w* \w covenant|strong="H01285"\w* \w for the generations to come|strong="H01755"\w*. \v 17 \w It|strong="H01931"\w* \w is a sign|strong="H00226"\w* \w between Me|strong="H00996"\w* \w and the Israelites|strong="H01121"\w* \w forever|strong="H05769"\w*; \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w in six|strong="H08337"\w* \w days|strong="H03117"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w made|strong="H06213"\w* \w the heavens|strong="H08064"\w* \w and the earth|strong="H00776"\w*, \w but on the seventh|strong="H07637"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w* \w He rested|strong="H07673"\w* \w and was refreshed|strong="H05314"\w*.’”
